meta {
  name: List Analytes
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{protocol}}://{{host}}:{{port}}/{{apiPrefix}}analytes?q=&kind=
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~q: ferritin
  ~kind: vital
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  The lab-analyte catalog (api.md → "Analytes"). Global to the household like medications, and
  populated by importing reports rather than a seed — expect an empty list before the first
  lab import. `q` is a case-insensitive substring over the printed name and the display name.

  `kind` selects which rows come back: `lab` (the default — ordinary lab analytes), `vital` (the
  five seeded vital signs, which carry each patient's normal ranges through the same range
  endpoints), or `all`. The default excludes vitals, so this request behaves exactly as it did
  before vitals joined the catalog.
}
